WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.502
-My first guest is the star of
"The Handmaid's Tale,"

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:06.506
which returns to Hulu
April 28th.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.541
Here is Elisabeth Moss!

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.609
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:13.046
-Oh! I'm so happy to see you.
Yeah!

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.681
Oh! I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.749
Thank you so much for
doing our show, pal.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:19.485
-Oh, my God.
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:22.155
It's so nice to see you.
-I know. It's good to see you.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.623
There's a lot to talk about.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.091
I want to talk about
"Handmaid's Tale."

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:28.160
But, first, I know you're
a giant Cubs fan,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.595
a Chicago Cubs fan.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:33.066
And you just finished filming
a movie with one of

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.902
the biggest Cubs fans
I know, Bill Murray.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.337
-Yes.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:41.908
-What -- Did you guys both,
like, go full-on fandom or...

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:45.311
-Bill Murray, for a Cubs fan --
he's like a God.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.046
Like, he's not just a Cubs fan.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:52.218
He's more important than most
players on the Cubs.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.353
-Yeah, they love him.
Absolutely. Yeah.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:57.223
-I didn't have the guts to
bring the Cubs up to him

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:01.694
until, literally, I was, like,
walking out with my bag,

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.229
and I ran into him
and I was like,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.665
"If I don't say something to
him, I'm gonna regret it."

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.200
-Yeah.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.771
-And then I kind of blacked out
and I just became a total moron

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:15.241
and was like,
"Uh, yeah, uh, Cubs are great.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.043
I'm a, you know, Cubs fan.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.412
Uh, yeah, they're
doing good this year."

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.681
It was so pathetic.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.350
-He was like, "What's going on?
What are you saying?"

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.718
-He was so nice.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.988
I'm sure he was like,
"What is she talking about?"

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.890
-Yeah.
-He was so lovely, though.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.426
-You've done high-pressure
things at Cubs games,

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.229
including something
I don't think I would ever do.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.230
You threw out the first pitch.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.365
Talk to me about this.
-Yeah.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.000
-Is that nerve-racking?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.569
Why -- I don't understand
why you would do it,

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:47.173
because I'm too afraid of --
Honestly, I would --

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.307
Questlove's done it.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.210
It was awful.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.411
-I heard about that.
-Oh, it was terrible.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.314
Like, the Phanatic
was making fun of him.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:56.315
Everything with the --
But it was like, you know,

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:57.450
Quest is just so lovable.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.918
So, he did it, and that was fun.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:02.054
But I would be afraid -- I mean,
I'd do it at Yankee Stadium.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.457
I'd be booed out of the city.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.793
-Yeah. I think
I was just excited

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:09.895
to be asked to do
anything by the Cubs.

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:11.263
I would never do it again.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:13.333
I think they've asked me to do
it again, and I won't.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.535
I've sung the 7th-inning stretch
three or four times.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.337
-"Take Me Out to the Ballgame"?

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:20.673
-Yes.
-That's nerve-racking, too!

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:23.042
I wouldn't do that either.
-That's fine.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.945
I mean, I get a little nervous,
but you have, like, you know,

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.481
30,000, 35,000 people
singing with you,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.049
and they don't care.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.383
They don't give
a [bleep] about you.

00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:33.352
They're like -- Like,
they're finishing their beer.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.188
They're thinking about
going home.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.422
Like, they don't care.
-They're all drunk.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.556
Yeah, okay.

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:39.492
Yeah, "Let's sing a song.
Why not?"

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.261
That's true.
-It's like, "What's happening?"

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.728
-Yeah.
-They don't care.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:45.164
So you're kind of just able to,
like, enjoy the experience,

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:48.968
but when I did the pitch,
I also sort of blacked out.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.603
And I was on "Mad Men"
at the time,

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.304
so they played
the "Mad Men" theme

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:55.275
when I was walking up to
the mound, which was so weird.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.342
-Yeah.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.810
-But I didn't bounce it.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.946
-You made it over the plate?
Strike?

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.347
-Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:04.016
-Amazing. Kudos to you.
I could never do that.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:05.652
Seriously,
I'm freaking out thinking --

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.885
even just thinking about it.

00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:09.655
I want to talk to you about
"Handmaid's Tale."

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:12.058
Season 4 is it now?

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.926
-Yeah, Season 4. Crazy.

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:17.930
-What can everyone
expect for this season?

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:25.571
-Again, more laughs,
more pratfalls, you know?

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:26.872
-Pratfalls and laughs
in this season.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.775
Oh, my goodness.
-Yep.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:31.644
Just a lot of bits.
-Wow!

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:34.613
-Surprise celebrity guests
coming in.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:37.250
"Hello!"
-Yes. Cameos galore.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.519
-Old car horns. Honk-honk.
Stuff like that.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.221
It's "Handmaid's Tale,"
of course.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:46.091
-You know, the usual.

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:49.528
Yeah, I mean, I do feel like
we have built something

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:52.365
over the past three seasons
that quite rightly

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.001
needs to be kind of fulfilled,

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.036
and I think that
we do that this season.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:04:00.072
With Season 4,
we kind of fulfill a lot of

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.775
the promises that we've made
over the last three years,

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.944
and we really get to see
not just June,

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:08.314
but a lot of these characters
really go to places

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:11.450
they've never gone before
and change dramatically.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.519
And it's a huge season,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:17.790
which, of course, we chose to
shoot during a pandemic,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.958
as you do.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.092
-I was going to ask
you about this,

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:22.061
because you made your
directorial debut.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.263
You directed
three of these episodes.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:27.700
And you chose the craziest time
to direct anything.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.771
Wow! You love pressure.
I think you like these things.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.273
You sing "Take Me Out to --"
You throw out the first pitch.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:35.575
I mean, why would you choose now

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:38.811
to direct your
first three episodes?

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:42.482
-I do love pressure,
but I didn't choose to --

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.817
You know, I chose
to direct the first --

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.653
Episode 3 that was going to be
my directorial debut

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:51.524
before COVID and started it.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:55.594
Then we shut down for
the six months, went back,

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:58.564
and then, all of a sudden,
I did that episode.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:02.201
I did two more.
I did episodes 8 and 9.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.103
I was like --
Because nobody else

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.106
was there a lot of the time,
like, the directors.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:10.643
Like, if a director finished
their work and left

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.178
and they didn't want
to come back

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:17.149
and quarantine for two weeks,
somebody had to direct it.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:18.717
So, all of a sudden,
I was, like,

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:22.154
the sort of director on hand.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.690
And it would be like,
"Lizzie, we got this, like,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.426
drone shot we need you to do.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:29.294
Would you mind just, like,
running out and grabbing that?"

00:05:29.294 --> 00:05:31.497
-Have you ever done a drone --
What does that even mean?

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.700
-No. I don't even know.
-That's great.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.336
-But by the end, we were joking
that I was just gonna be this,

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:41.440
like, journeyman director now,
like, off to do my ninth,

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.008
you know, episode of
"Law &amp; Order"

00:05:43.008 --> 00:05:45.177
and just
clocking in, clocking out.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:47.346
-Of course.
I could see more of this.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:48.514
I'm telling you, man.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.082
I want to show everyone a clip

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:51.617
from an episode
that you directed.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.320
Here's Elisabeth Moss in
"The Handmaid's Tale."

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.521
Take a look.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.224
-Well...

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:01.260
it's so wonderful being all
together again, isn't it, yeah?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.862
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:06.232
-♪ All these things
into position ♪

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:10.169
♪ All these things
we'll one day swallow whole ♪

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.904
♪♪

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:23.315
♪ And fade out

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:29.755
again ♪

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:34.694
♪ And fade out ♪

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:37.196
-Yes! That's what I'm
talking about!

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:38.330
Come on!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.401
Yeah, that was great!
Elisabeth Moss!

